1
00:00:02,260 --> 00:00:06,279
Chapter 28 Two days are passed.

2
00:00:06,980 --> 00:00:08,459
It is a summer evening.

3
00:00:09,339 --> 00:00:11,980
The coachman has set me down at a place called Whitcross.

4
00:00:13,040 --> 00:00:16,281
He could take me no farther for the summer I had given,

5
00:00:16,283 --> 00:00:19,279
and I was not possessed of another shilling in the world.

6
00:00:20,160 --> 00:00:22,120
The coach is a mile off by this time.

7
00:00:22,919 --> 00:00:23,919
I am alone.

8
00:00:24,360 --> 00:00:28,110
At this moment, I discovered that I forgot to take my parcel out

9
00:00:28,110 --> 00:00:31,680
of the pocket of the coach, where I had placed it for safety.

10
00:00:32,620 --> 00:00:39,019
There it remains, there it must remain, and now I am absolutely destitute.

11
00:00:39,819 --> 00:00:42,540
Whitcross is no town, nor even a hamlet.

12
00:00:43,339 --> 00:00:48,239
It is but a stone pillar set up where four roads meet, whitewashed, I suppose,

13
00:00:48,519 --> 00:00:50,980
to be more obvious at a distance and in darkness.

14
00:00:51,940 --> 00:00:57,580
Four arms spring from its summit, the nearest town to which these point is,

15
00:00:57,639 --> 00:01:03,440
according to the inscription, distant 10 miles, the farthest above 20.

16
00:01:04,139 --> 00:01:09,260
From the well-known names of these towns, I learn in what county I have lighted,

17
00:01:09,580 --> 00:01:14,639
a North Midland Shire, dusk with Mauland, ridged with mountain.

18
00:01:15,760 --> 00:01:16,959
This I see.

19
00:01:18,360 --> 00:01:22,305
There are great moors behind, and on each hand of me, there

20
00:01:22,305 --> 00:01:26,139
are waves of mountains far beyond that deep valley at my feet.

21
00:01:27,339 --> 00:01:31,260
The population here must be thin, and I see no passengers on these roads.

22
00:01:32,099 --> 00:01:37,779
They stretch out east, west, north, and south, white, broad, lonely.

23
00:01:38,419 --> 00:01:41,038
They are all cut in the moor, and the Heather

24
00:01:41,040 --> 00:01:44,360
grows deep and wild to their very verge.

25
00:01:44,919 --> 00:01:50,739
Yet a chance traveler might pass by, and I wish no eye to see me now.

26
00:01:51,699 --> 00:01:56,239
Strangers would wonder what I am doing, lingering here at the signpost,

27
00:01:56,819 --> 00:01:58,839
evidently objectless and lost.

28
00:01:59,660 --> 00:02:01,080
I might be questioned.

29
00:02:01,879 --> 00:02:07,419
I could give no answer, but what would sound incredible and excite suspicion.

30
00:02:08,440 --> 00:02:11,440
Not a tie holds me to human society at this moment.

31
00:02:12,220 --> 00:02:17,319
Not a charm or hope calls me where my fellow creatures are, none that saw me

32
00:02:17,321 --> 00:02:21,160
would have a kind thought, or a good wish for me.

33
00:02:21,819 --> 00:02:25,300
I have no relative but the universal mother, nature.

34
00:02:26,080 --> 00:02:28,559
I will seek her breast and ask repose.

35
00:02:29,440 --> 00:02:31,639
I struck straight into the heath.

36
00:02:32,220 --> 00:02:36,699
I held onto a hollow I saw deeply following the brown moor side.

37
00:02:37,300 --> 00:02:39,739
I waded knee deep in its dark growth.

38
00:02:40,500 --> 00:02:43,756
I turned with its turnings, and finding a moss-blackened

39
00:02:43,756 --> 00:02:47,559
granite crag in a hidden angle, I sat down under it.

40
00:02:48,419 --> 00:02:50,480
High banks of moor were about me.

41
00:02:51,199 --> 00:02:52,779
The crag protected my head.

42
00:02:52,860 --> 00:02:54,720
The sky was over that.

43
00:02:55,919 --> 00:02:59,419
Some time passed before I felt tranquil even here.

44
00:03:00,279 --> 00:03:04,027
I had a vague dread that wild cattle might be near,

45
00:03:04,027 --> 00:03:07,300
or that some sportsman or poacher might discover me.

46
00:03:07,879 --> 00:03:13,300
If a gust of wind swept the waste, I looked up, fearing it was the rush of a ball.

47
00:03:13,699 --> 00:03:16,540
If a plover whistled, I imagined it a man.

48
00:03:18,440 --> 00:03:22,364
Finding my apprehensions unfounded, however, and calmed

49
00:03:22,366 --> 00:03:25,260
by the deep silence the rain does evening decline.

50
00:03:25,839 --> 00:03:28,160
At nightfall, I took confidence.

51
00:03:29,000 --> 00:03:30,819
As yet, I had not thought.

52
00:03:31,620 --> 00:03:34,639
I had only listened, watched, dreaded.

53
00:03:35,419 --> 00:03:37,819
Now I regained the faculty of reflection.

54
00:03:38,279 --> 00:03:40,059
What was I to do, where to go?

55
00:03:41,160 --> 00:03:45,819
Oh, intolerable questions, when I could do nothing and go nowhere.

56
00:03:46,639 --> 00:03:50,713
When a long way must yet be measured by my weary,

57
00:03:50,714 --> 00:03:54,180
trembling limbs before I could reach human habitation.

58
00:03:54,699 --> 00:03:58,366
When cold charity must be entreated before I

59
00:03:58,368 --> 00:04:02,701
could get a lodging, reluctant sympathy important.

60
00:04:03,279 --> 00:04:06,951
Almost certain repulse incurred before my tail

61
00:04:06,953 --> 00:04:10,639
could be listened to, or one of my wants relieved.

62
00:04:11,260 --> 00:04:12,680
I touched the heath.

63
00:04:13,440 --> 00:04:16,639
It was dry and yet warm, with the heat of the summer day.

64
00:04:17,500 --> 00:04:18,500
I looked at the sky.

65
00:04:19,260 --> 00:04:20,260
It was pure.

66
00:04:20,800 --> 00:04:23,440
A kindly star twinkle just above the chasm ridge.

67
00:04:24,360 --> 00:04:29,360
The dew fell, but with propitious softness, no breeze whispered.

68
00:04:30,220 --> 00:04:32,139
Nature seemed to me benign and good.

69
00:04:32,940 --> 00:04:35,099
I thought she loved me, outcast as I was.

70
00:04:35,959 --> 00:04:40,402
And I, who from man could anticipate only mistrust

71
00:04:40,402 --> 00:04:44,419
rejection, insult, clung to her with filial fondness.

72
00:04:45,419 --> 00:04:49,980
Tonight, at least, I would be her guest as I was her child.

73
00:04:50,980 --> 00:04:53,800
My mother would lodge me without money and without price.

74
00:04:55,180 --> 00:04:58,120
I had one morsel of bread yet.

75
00:04:59,239 --> 00:05:01,546
The remnant of a roll I'd bought in a town we passed

76
00:05:01,548 --> 00:05:05,040
through at noon with a stray penny, my last coin.

77
00:05:06,519 --> 00:05:12,239
I saw ripe bilberies gleaming here and there, like jet beads in the heath.

78
00:05:12,580 --> 00:05:15,360
I gathered a handful and ate them with the bread.

79
00:05:16,180 --> 00:05:22,680
My hunger, sharp before, was if not satisfied, appeased by this hermit's meal.

80
00:05:23,559 --> 00:05:28,199
I said my evening prayers at its conclusion and then chose my couch.

81
00:05:29,080 --> 00:05:32,019
Beside the crag, the heath was very deep.

82
00:05:32,879 --> 00:05:35,199
When I lay down my feet were buried in it.

83
00:05:35,800 --> 00:05:41,019
Rising high on each side, it left only a narrow space for the night air to invade.

84
00:05:41,879 --> 00:05:46,080
I folded my shawl double and spread it over me for a coverlet.

85
00:05:46,980 --> 00:05:49,440
A low mossy swell was my pillow.

86
00:05:50,239 --> 00:05:55,580
Thus lodged I was not, at least at the commencement of the night, cold.

87
00:05:56,580 --> 00:06:00,959
My rest might have been blissful enough, only a sad heart broke it.

88
00:06:01,760 --> 00:06:06,959
It plained of its gaping wounds, its inward bleeding, its riven cords,

89
00:06:08,000 --> 00:06:10,360
it trembled for Mr. Rochester and his doom.

90
00:06:11,300 --> 00:06:15,819
It bemoaned him with bitter pity, it demanded him with ceaseless longing,

91
00:06:16,360 --> 00:06:20,578
and impotent as a bird with both wings broken, it still

92
00:06:20,580 --> 00:06:25,599
quivered its shattered opinions in vain attempts to seek him.

93
00:06:26,680 --> 00:06:31,319
Worn out with this torture of thought, I rose to my knees.

94
00:06:32,639 --> 00:06:36,944
Night was come and her planets were risen, a safe

95
00:06:36,946 --> 00:06:40,500
still night, too serene for the companionship of fear.

96
00:06:41,360 --> 00:06:46,819
We know that God is everywhere, but certainly we feel his presence most

97
00:06:46,821 --> 00:06:51,900
when his works are on the grandest scale spread before us, and it is in the

98
00:06:51,900 --> 00:06:57,379
unclouded night sky, where his worlds wheel their silent course, that we read

99
00:06:57,381 --> 00:07:02,559
clearest, his infinitude, his omnipotence, his omnipresence.

100
00:07:03,199 --> 00:07:06,300
I had risen to my knees to pray for Mr. Rochester.

101
00:07:07,680 --> 00:07:14,919
Looking up, I, with tear-dimmed eyes, saw the mighty Milky Way, remembering what

102
00:07:14,921 --> 00:07:19,839
it was, what countless systems their swept space like a soft trace of light.

103
00:07:20,879 --> 00:07:24,552
I felt the might and strength of God, sure as I of

104
00:07:24,552 --> 00:07:28,339
his efficiency to save what he had made, convinced.

105
00:07:29,220 --> 00:07:33,419
I grew that neither earth should perish nor one of the souls it treasured.

106
00:07:34,080 --> 00:07:35,739
I turned my prayer to Thanksgiving.

107
00:07:36,720 --> 00:07:39,919
The source of life was also the savior of spirits.

108
00:07:40,860 --> 00:07:45,160
Mr. Rochester was safe, he was God's and by God would he be guarded.

109
00:07:46,220 --> 00:07:52,279
I again nestled to the breast of the hill, and air long in sleep for God's sorrow.

110
00:07:52,959 --> 00:07:59,300
But next day, want came to me pale and bare, long after the little birds had left

111
00:07:59,300 --> 00:08:05,239
their nests, long after bees had come in the sweet prime of day, to gather the

112
00:08:05,241 --> 00:08:09,839
heath -honey before the dew was dried, when the long morning shadows were

113
00:08:09,841 --> 00:08:13,059
curtailed, and the sun filled earth and sky.

114
00:08:13,940 --> 00:08:16,559
I got up, and I looked around me.

115
00:08:17,639 --> 00:08:19,959
What a still hot, perfect day.

116
00:08:20,839 --> 00:08:24,940
What a golden desert this spreading more, everywhere sunshine.

117
00:08:25,800 --> 00:08:27,860
I wished I could live in it and on it.

118
00:08:28,959 --> 00:08:31,059
I saw a lizard run over the crag.

119
00:08:31,660 --> 00:08:34,339
I saw a bee busy among the sweet billberries.

120
00:08:35,099 --> 00:08:38,315
I would feign at the moment have become bee or lizard, that

121
00:08:38,317 --> 00:08:42,319
I might have found fitting nutriment, permanent shelter here.

122
00:08:43,099 --> 00:08:47,300
But I was a human being and had a human beings once.

123
00:08:48,080 --> 00:08:51,839
I must not linger where there was nothing to supply them.

124
00:08:52,400 --> 00:08:53,400
I rose.

125
00:08:53,819 --> 00:08:55,839
I looked back at the bed I had left.

126
00:08:56,779 --> 00:09:03,360
Hopeless of the future, I wished but this, that my maker had that night thought good

127
00:09:03,360 --> 00:09:09,559
to require my soul of me while I slept, and that this weary frame absolved by

128
00:09:09,561 --> 00:09:14,578
death from further conflict with fate, had now but to decay

129
00:09:14,580 --> 00:09:18,220
quietly and mingle in peace with the soil of this wilderness.

130
00:09:19,459 --> 00:09:23,860
Life, however, was yet in my possession with all

131
00:09:23,862 --> 00:09:27,360
its requirements and pains and responsibilities.

132
00:09:28,040 --> 00:09:29,480
The burden must be carried.

133
00:09:30,260 --> 00:09:31,540
The want provided for.

134
00:09:32,199 --> 00:09:33,379
The suffering endured.

135
00:09:34,360 --> 00:09:35,620
The responsibility fulfilled.

136
00:09:36,739 --> 00:09:37,739
I set out.

137
00:09:38,059 --> 00:09:39,360
Whit cross regained.

138
00:09:40,000 --> 00:09:43,779
I followed a road which led from the sun, now fervent and high.

139
00:09:44,839 --> 00:09:47,940
By no other circumstance had I will to decide my choice.

140
00:09:48,839 --> 00:09:50,180
I walked a long time.

141
00:09:51,059 --> 00:09:55,580
And when I thought I had nearly done enough, and might conscientiously yield to

142
00:09:55,580 --> 00:10:00,879
the fatigue that almost overpowered me, might relax this forced action.

143
00:10:01,360 --> 00:10:05,652
And, sitting down on a stone I saw near, submit

144
00:10:05,654 --> 00:10:09,639
resistlessly to the apathy that clogged heart and limb.

145
00:10:10,660 --> 00:10:12,620
I heard a bell chime, a church bell.

146
00:10:13,459 --> 00:10:18,980
I turned in the direction of the sound, and there, amongst the romantic hills

147
00:10:18,980 --> 00:10:21,754
whose changes and aspect I had ceased to

148
00:10:21,754 --> 00:10:25,821
note an hour ago, I saw a hamlet and a spire.

149
00:10:26,220 --> 00:10:32,381
All the valley at my right hand was full of pasture fields and corn fields and wood.

150
00:10:32,540 --> 00:10:38,059
And a glittering stream ran zigzag through the varied shades of green, the mellowing

151
00:10:38,061 --> 00:10:42,180
grain, the somber woodland, the clear and sunny Lee.

152
00:10:43,139 --> 00:10:48,220
Recalled by the rumbling of wheels to the road before me, I saw a heavily laden

153
00:10:48,220 --> 00:10:53,500
wagon laboring up the hill, and not far beyond were two cows and their drover.

154
00:10:54,519 --> 00:10:56,839
Human life and human labour were near.

155
00:10:57,800 --> 00:11:02,660
I must struggle on, strive to live and bend to toil like the rest.

156
00:11:03,879 --> 00:11:06,279
About two o'clock PM I entered the village.

157
00:11:07,300 --> 00:11:10,105
At the bottom of its one street there was a little

158
00:11:10,107 --> 00:11:13,101
shop with some cakes of bread in the window.

159
00:11:13,199 --> 00:11:15,360
I coveted a cake of bread.

160
00:11:16,500 --> 00:11:20,279
With that refreshment I could perhaps regain a degree of energy.

161
00:11:21,059 --> 00:11:24,279
Without it, it would be difficult to proceed.

162
00:11:25,400 --> 00:11:29,057
The wish to have some strength and some vigor returned

163
00:11:29,059 --> 00:11:31,919
to me as soon as I was amongst my fellow beings.

164
00:11:32,860 --> 00:11:37,760
I felt it would be degrading to faint with hunger on the cause way of a hamlet.

165
00:11:38,400 --> 00:11:42,660
Had I nothing about me I could offer in exchange for one of these roles?

166
00:11:43,959 --> 00:11:44,959
I considered.

167
00:11:46,040 --> 00:11:49,580
I had a small silk hankerchief tied around my throat.

168
00:11:50,300 --> 00:11:51,300
I had my gloves.

169
00:11:52,180 --> 00:11:57,739
I could hardly tell how men and women in extremities of destitution proceeded.

170
00:11:58,720 --> 00:12:02,739
I did not know whether either of these articles would be accepted.

171
00:12:03,559 --> 00:12:06,959
Probably they would not, but I must try.

172
00:12:08,500 --> 00:12:09,620
I entered the shop.

173
00:12:10,739 --> 00:12:11,739
A woman was there.

174
00:12:13,160 --> 00:12:16,597
Seeing a respectively dressed person, a lady as

175
00:12:16,597 --> 00:12:19,781
she supposed, she came forward with civility.

176
00:12:20,559 --> 00:12:21,720
How could she serve me?

177
00:12:22,339 --> 00:12:23,739
I was seized with shame.

178
00:12:24,559 --> 00:12:27,440
My tongue would not utter the request I had prepared.

179
00:12:28,180 --> 00:12:32,620
I dared not offer her the half-worn gloves, the creased hankerchief.

180
00:12:33,099 --> 00:12:35,620
Besides, I felt it would be absurd.

181
00:12:36,779 --> 00:12:40,339
I only begged permission to sit down a moment as I was tired.

182
00:12:41,279 --> 00:12:46,601
Disappointed in the expectation of a customer, she coolly exceeded to my request.

183
00:12:47,139 --> 00:12:48,139
She pointed to a seat.

184
00:12:48,800 --> 00:12:49,800
I sank into it.

185
00:12:50,279 --> 00:12:52,660
I felt sorely urged to weep.

186
00:12:53,419 --> 00:12:58,379
But conscious how unseasonable such a manifestation would be, I restrained it.

187
00:12:59,000 --> 00:13:04,980
Soon, I asked her, if there were any dressmaker or plain workwoman in the village.

188
00:13:05,180 --> 00:13:09,419
Yes, two or three, quite as many as there was employment for.

189
00:13:10,480 --> 00:13:11,599
I reflected.

190
00:13:12,279 --> 00:13:14,139
I was driven to the point now.

191
00:13:14,760 --> 00:13:17,819
I was brought face to face with necessity.

192
00:13:18,940 --> 00:13:25,580
I stood in the position of one without a resource, without a friend, without a coin.

193
00:13:25,620 --> 00:13:26,680
I must do something.

194
00:13:27,160 --> 00:13:27,279
What?

195
00:13:27,839 --> 00:13:29,000
I must apply somewhere.

196
00:13:29,400 --> 00:13:30,400
Where?

197
00:13:31,199 --> 00:13:34,699
Did she know of any place in the neighborhood where a servant was wanted?

198
00:13:35,839 --> 00:13:37,220
Nay, she couldn't say.

199
00:13:38,559 --> 00:13:40,279
What was the chief trade in this place?

200
00:13:41,139 --> 00:13:42,699
What did most of the people do?

201
00:13:43,819 --> 00:13:46,786
Some were farm laborers, a good deal worked at

202
00:13:46,786 --> 00:13:49,800
Mr. Oliver's needle factory and at the foundry.

203
00:13:50,599 --> 00:13:52,500
Did Mr. Oliver employ women?

204
00:13:53,620 --> 00:13:55,019
Nay, it was men's work.

205
00:13:55,980 --> 00:13:57,080
And what did the women do?

206
00:13:58,319 --> 00:13:59,919
Inault was the answer.

207
00:14:01,239 --> 00:14:03,099
Some does one thing and some another.

208
00:14:03,699 --> 00:14:05,580
Poor folkmen get on as they can.

209
00:14:06,860 --> 00:14:08,620
She seemed to be tired of my questions.

210
00:14:09,459 --> 00:14:13,099
And indeed, what claim had I to importune her?

211
00:14:13,860 --> 00:14:15,120
A neighbor or two came in.

212
00:14:15,839 --> 00:14:17,540
My chair was evidently wanted.

213
00:14:17,900 --> 00:14:18,900
I took leave.

214
00:14:19,139 --> 00:14:21,841
I passed up the street, looking as I went at all

215
00:14:21,841 --> 00:14:25,101
the houses to the right hand and to the left.

216
00:14:25,379 --> 00:14:29,980
But I could discover no pretext, nor see an inducement to enter any.

217
00:14:31,080 --> 00:14:34,591
I rambled around the hamlet, going sometimes to a

218
00:14:34,593 --> 00:14:38,080
little distance and returning again for an hour or more.

219
00:14:39,279 --> 00:14:43,639
Much exhausted and suffering greatly now for want of food.

220
00:14:44,440 --> 00:14:48,440
I turned aside into a lane and sat down under the hedge.

221
00:14:49,620 --> 00:14:51,480
Air many minutes had elapsed.

222
00:14:51,779 --> 00:14:56,419
I was again on my feet, however, and again searching something,

223
00:14:56,940 --> 00:15:00,099
a resource or at least an informant.

224
00:15:00,800 --> 00:15:05,959
A pretty little house stood at the top of the lane, with a garden before it,

225
00:15:06,580 --> 00:15:09,379
exquisitely neat and brilliantly blooming.

226
00:15:10,000 --> 00:15:11,000
I stopped at it.

227
00:15:11,680 --> 00:15:15,580
What business had I to approach the white door or touch the glittering knocker?

228
00:15:16,620 --> 00:15:19,667
In what way could it possibly be the interest

229
00:15:19,669 --> 00:15:23,419
of the inhabitants of that dwelling to serve me?

230
00:15:24,779 --> 00:15:27,519
Yet, I drew near and knocked.

231
00:15:28,559 --> 00:15:32,540
A mild-looking, cleanly-attired young woman opened the door.

232
00:15:33,319 --> 00:15:37,720
In such a voice as might be expected from a hopeless heart and fainting frame,

233
00:15:38,480 --> 00:15:43,900
a voice wretchedly low and faltering, I asked if a servant was wanted here.

234
00:15:44,940 --> 00:15:48,379
No, said she, we do not keep a servant.

235
00:15:49,319 --> 00:15:52,500
Can you tell me where I could get employment of any kind?

236
00:15:53,300 --> 00:15:54,300
I continued.

237
00:15:54,599 --> 00:15:57,519
I am a stranger without acquaintance in this place.

238
00:15:58,180 --> 00:16:00,180
I want some work, no matter what.

239
00:16:01,419 --> 00:16:05,839
But it was not her business to think for me or to seek a place for me.

240
00:16:06,980 --> 00:16:13,940
Besides, in her eyes, how doubtful must have appeared my character, position, tail.

241
00:16:14,199 --> 00:16:15,199
She shook her head.

242
00:16:15,620 --> 00:16:18,459
She was sorry she could give me no information.

243
00:16:19,160 --> 00:16:23,860
And the white door closed, quite gently and civilly, but it shut me out.

244
00:16:25,120 --> 00:16:28,250
If she had held it open a little longer, I believe I should

245
00:16:28,250 --> 00:16:31,480
have begged a piece of bread, for I was now brought low.

246
00:16:32,919 --> 00:16:36,552
I could not bear to return to the sordid village,

247
00:16:36,553 --> 00:16:39,980
where besides no prospect of aid was visible.

248
00:16:40,319 --> 00:16:46,319
I should have longed rather to deviate to a wood I saw not far off, which appeared

249
00:16:46,321 --> 00:16:49,480
in its thick shade to offer inviting shelter.

250
00:16:50,239 --> 00:16:56,400
But I was so sick, so weak, so nored with nature's cravings.

251
00:16:56,599 --> 00:17:00,480
Instinct kept me roaming round the boats where there was a chance of food.

252
00:17:01,480 --> 00:17:06,980
Solitude would be no solitude, rest no rest, while the vulture hunger,

253
00:17:07,639 --> 00:17:10,099
thus sank beak and talons in my side.

254
00:17:11,040 --> 00:17:16,580
I drew near houses, I left them and came back again, and again I wandered away,

255
00:17:16,860 --> 00:17:21,156
always repelled by the consciousness of having no claim

256
00:17:21,158 --> 00:17:25,419
to ask, no right to expect interest in my isolated lot.

257
00:17:26,919 --> 00:17:32,040
Meantime, the afternoon advanced, while I thus wandered about like a lost

258
00:17:32,040 --> 00:17:37,139
and starving dog, in crossing a field I saw the church spire before me.

259
00:17:38,019 --> 00:17:39,440
I hastened towards it.

260
00:17:40,860 --> 00:17:46,739
Near the churchyard, and in the middle of a garden, stood a well built, though small

261
00:17:46,741 --> 00:17:50,580
house, which I had no doubt was the parsinage.

262
00:17:51,300 --> 00:17:57,139
I remembered that strangers who arrive at a place where they have no friends and who

263
00:17:57,141 --> 00:18:02,839
want employment, sometimes apply to the clergyman for introduction and aid.

264
00:18:03,800 --> 00:18:07,972
It is the clergyman's function to help, at least

265
00:18:07,974 --> 00:18:11,561
with advice, those who wished to help themselves.

266
00:18:12,900 --> 00:18:16,639
I seem to have something like a right to seek council here.

267
00:18:17,980 --> 00:18:23,819
Renewing, then, my courage, and gathering my feeble remains of strength I pushed on,

268
00:18:24,559 --> 00:18:27,419
I reached the house and knocked at the kitchen door.

269
00:18:28,599 --> 00:18:29,839
An old woman opened.

270
00:18:30,500 --> 00:18:32,480
I asked, was this the parsinage?

271
00:18:33,180 --> 00:18:34,180
Yes.

272
00:18:34,620 --> 00:18:35,680
Was the clergyman in?

273
00:18:36,180 --> 00:18:36,379
No.

274
00:18:37,139 --> 00:18:38,260
Would he be in soon?

275
00:18:38,860 --> 00:18:39,040
No.

276
00:18:39,519 --> 00:18:41,500
He was gone from home, to a distance?

277
00:18:42,779 --> 00:18:44,180
Not so far.

278
00:18:44,879 --> 00:18:46,419
Happened three mile.

279
00:18:47,199 --> 00:18:50,379
He had been called away by the sudden death of his father.

280
00:18:51,059 --> 00:18:56,059
He was at marsh end now and would very likely stay there a fortnight longer.

281
00:18:57,000 --> 00:18:58,580
Was there any lady of the house?

282
00:18:59,559 --> 00:19:03,160
Nay, there was not but her, and she was housekeeper.

283
00:19:03,980 --> 00:19:06,940
And of her, reader, I could not bear to ask

284
00:19:06,940 --> 00:19:10,480
the relief for one of which I was sinking.

285
00:19:10,620 --> 00:19:11,620
I could not yet beg.

286
00:19:12,360 --> 00:19:14,199
And again, I crawled away.

287
00:19:15,260 --> 00:19:17,319
Once more, I took off my handkerchief.

288
00:19:18,160 --> 00:19:21,000
Once more, I thought of the cakes of bread in the little shop.

289
00:19:22,260 --> 00:19:23,540
Oh, for but a crust.

290
00:19:24,500 --> 00:19:27,080
For but one mouthful to lay the pang of famine.

291
00:19:28,139 --> 00:19:31,019
Instinctively, I turned my face again to the village.

292
00:19:31,580 --> 00:19:32,900
I found the shop again.

293
00:19:33,699 --> 00:19:34,699
And I went in.

294
00:19:35,360 --> 00:19:39,459
And though others were there, besides the woman, I ventured the request.

295
00:19:40,379 --> 00:19:42,279
Would she give me a role for this handkerchief?

296
00:19:43,239 --> 00:19:45,519
She looked at me with evidence suspicion.

297
00:19:46,419 --> 00:19:48,779
Nay, she never sold stuff with that way.

298
00:19:49,879 --> 00:19:50,919
Almost desperate.

299
00:19:51,339 --> 00:19:52,599
I asked for half a cake.

300
00:19:53,239 --> 00:19:54,339
She again refused.

301
00:19:54,919 --> 00:19:57,599
How could she tell where I had got the handkerchief?

302
00:19:58,199 --> 00:19:59,199
She said.

303
00:19:59,680 --> 00:20:00,680
Would she take my gloves?

304
00:20:01,480 --> 00:20:02,480
No.

305
00:20:02,879 --> 00:20:04,260
What could she do with them?

306
00:20:05,419 --> 00:20:06,419
Reader.

307
00:20:06,779 --> 00:20:09,319
It is not pleasant to dwell on these details.

308
00:20:10,059 --> 00:20:14,300
Some say, there is enjoyment in looking back to painful experience past.

309
00:20:15,040 --> 00:20:20,760
But at this day, I can scarcely bear to review the times to which I allude.

310
00:20:21,599 --> 00:20:27,379
The moral degradation, blent with the physical suffering, formed to distressing

311
00:20:27,381 --> 00:20:30,900
a recollection ever to be willingly dwelt on.

312
00:20:31,819 --> 00:20:34,059
I blamed none of those who repulsed me.

313
00:20:34,879 --> 00:20:39,319
I felt it was what was to be expected, and what could not be helped.

314
00:20:40,360 --> 00:20:43,476
An ordinary beggar is frequently an object of

315
00:20:43,476 --> 00:20:46,980
suspicion, a well-dressed beggar inevitably so.

316
00:20:47,879 --> 00:20:50,440
To be sure, what I begged was employment.

317
00:20:51,459 --> 00:20:54,300
But whose business was it to provide me with employment?

318
00:20:55,500 --> 00:20:59,404
Not certainly that of persons who saw me then for the

319
00:20:59,406 --> 00:21:03,099
first time, and who knew nothing about my character.

320
00:21:03,919 --> 00:21:09,040
And as to the woman who would not take my handkerchief in exchange for her bread,

321
00:21:09,699 --> 00:21:12,982
why she was right, if the offer appeared to

322
00:21:12,983 --> 00:21:16,559
her sinister, or the exchange unprofitable.

323
00:21:17,419 --> 00:21:20,959
Let me condense now, I am sick of the subject.

324
00:21:21,779 --> 00:21:26,879
A little before dark, I passed a farmhouse, at the open door of which the

325
00:21:26,881 --> 00:21:30,260
farmer was sitting, eating his supper of bread and cheese.

326
00:21:31,620 --> 00:21:37,860
I stopped and said, will you give me a piece of bread, for I am very hungry.

327
00:21:39,199 --> 00:21:43,516
He cast on me a glance of surprise, but without answering,

328
00:21:43,516 --> 00:21:46,459
he cut a thick slice from his loaf and gave it to me.

329
00:21:48,559 --> 00:21:52,705
I imagine he did not think I was a beggar, but only an

330
00:21:52,707 --> 00:21:57,059
eccentric sort of lady who had taken a fancy to his brown loaf.

331
00:21:58,139 --> 00:22:02,360
As soon as I was out of sight of his house, I sat down and ate it.

332
00:22:03,620 --> 00:22:06,300
I could not hope to get a lodging under a roof,

333
00:22:06,300 --> 00:22:09,059
and sort it in the wood I have before alluded to.

334
00:22:09,879 --> 00:22:16,660
But my night was wretched, my rest broken, the ground was damp, the air cold.

335
00:22:17,599 --> 00:22:21,154
Besides, intruders passed near me more than once,

336
00:22:21,154 --> 00:22:24,040
and I had again and again to change my quarters.

337
00:22:24,620 --> 00:22:27,360
No sense of safety or tranquility befriended me.

338
00:22:29,000 --> 00:22:33,419
Towards morning, it rained, the whole of the following day was wet.

339
00:22:34,580 --> 00:22:40,379
Do not ask me, reader, to give a minute account of that day, as before I sought

340
00:22:40,381 --> 00:22:45,839
work, as before I was repulsed, as before I starved.

341
00:22:46,660 --> 00:22:51,239
But once did food pass my lips, at the door of a cottage I saw a little

342
00:22:51,241 --> 00:22:54,639
girl about to throw a mess of cold porridge into a pig trough.

343
00:22:55,519 --> 00:22:56,720
Will you give me that?

344
00:22:57,199 --> 00:22:58,199
I asked.

345
00:22:58,239 --> 00:22:59,239
She stared at me.

346
00:22:59,819 --> 00:23:01,379
Mother, she exclaimed.

347
00:23:02,059 --> 00:23:04,459
There is a woman wants me to give her these porridge.

348
00:23:05,959 --> 00:23:08,440
Well, lass, replied a voice within.

349
00:23:09,620 --> 00:23:12,580
Give it her if she's a beggar, to pig doesn't want it.

350
00:23:13,760 --> 00:23:19,360
The girl emptied the stiffened mold into my hand, and I devoured it ravenously.

351
00:23:20,639 --> 00:23:24,512
As the wet twilight deepened, I stopped in a solitary

352
00:23:24,514 --> 00:23:27,779
bridal path, which I had been pursuing an hour or more.

353
00:23:29,099 --> 00:23:32,440
My strength is quite failing me, I said, in a soliloquy.

354
00:23:33,059 --> 00:23:34,599
I feel I cannot go much farther.

355
00:23:35,739 --> 00:23:37,599
Shall I be an outcast again this night?

356
00:23:38,739 --> 00:23:43,400
While the rain descends so must I lay my head on the cold, drenched ground.

357
00:23:44,580 --> 00:23:48,800
I fear I cannot do otherwise, for who will receive me?

358
00:23:49,940 --> 00:23:55,099
But it will be very dreadful, with this feeling of hunger, faintness, chill,

359
00:23:55,559 --> 00:24:00,459
and this sense of desolation, this total prostration of hope.

360
00:24:01,819 --> 00:24:05,500
In all likelihood, though, I should die before morning.

361
00:24:06,580 --> 00:24:09,379
And why cannot I reconcile myself to the prospect of death?

362
00:24:10,199 --> 00:24:12,879
Why do I struggle to retain a valueless life?

363
00:24:13,360 --> 00:24:17,360
Because I know, or believe, Mr. Rochester is living.

364
00:24:18,160 --> 00:24:24,021
And then, to die of want and cold is a fate to which nature cannot submit passively.

365
00:24:24,180 --> 00:24:29,080
Oh, Providence, sustain me a little longer, aid direct me.

366
00:24:30,760 --> 00:24:34,379
My glazed eye wandered over the dim and misty landscape.

367
00:24:35,319 --> 00:24:37,620
I saw I had strayed far from the village.

368
00:24:38,199 --> 00:24:39,500
It was quite out of sight.

369
00:24:40,279 --> 00:24:42,800
The very cultivation surrounding it had disappeared.

370
00:24:43,639 --> 00:24:50,080
I had, by crossways and by paths, once more drawn near the tract of Moorland.

371
00:24:50,400 --> 00:24:57,199
And now, only a few fields, almost as wild and unproductive as the heath from which

372
00:24:57,201 --> 00:25:02,699
they were scarcely reclaimed lay between me and the dusky hill.

373
00:25:03,819 --> 00:25:10,000
Well, I would rather die younger than in a street or on a frequented road,

374
00:25:10,819 --> 00:25:11,819
I reflected.

375
00:25:12,400 --> 00:25:18,300
And far better that crows and ravens, if any ravens there be in these regions,

376
00:25:19,000 --> 00:25:23,540
should pick my flesh from my bones than that they should be prisoned in a

377
00:25:23,540 --> 00:25:27,419
workhouse coffin and molder in a pauper's grave.

378
00:25:28,540 --> 00:25:30,360
To the hill then, I turned.

379
00:25:31,279 --> 00:25:32,279
I reached it.

380
00:25:32,900 --> 00:25:35,675
It remained now only to find a hollow where I could

381
00:25:35,675 --> 00:25:39,720
lie down and feel at least hidden, if not secure.

382
00:25:40,639 --> 00:25:43,059
But all the surface of the waste looked level.

383
00:25:43,940 --> 00:25:49,639
It showed no variation but of tint, green, where Russian moss overgrew the

384
00:25:49,641 --> 00:25:53,919
marshes, black, where the dry soil bore only heath.

385
00:25:54,760 --> 00:26:00,360
Dark as it was getting, I could still see these changes, though but as mere

386
00:26:00,360 --> 00:26:05,319
alternations of light and shade, for colour had faded with the daylight.

387
00:26:06,540 --> 00:26:11,699
My eye still roved over the sullen swell and along the more edge, vanishing amidst

388
00:26:11,701 --> 00:26:17,599
the wildest scenery, when at one dim point far in among the marshes and the ridges,

389
00:26:18,300 --> 00:26:19,860
a light sprang up.

390
00:26:21,040 --> 00:26:23,553
That is an igneous fatuous, was my first

391
00:26:23,555 --> 00:26:27,281
thought, and I expected it would soon vanish.

392
00:26:27,720 --> 00:26:32,760
It burnt on, however, quite steadily, neither receding nor advancing.

393
00:26:33,940 --> 00:26:37,180
Is it then a bonfire just kindled, I questioned?

394
00:26:37,739 --> 00:26:41,529
I watched to see whether it would spread but no,

395
00:26:41,531 --> 00:26:45,599
as it did not diminish so it did not enlarge.

396
00:26:46,339 --> 00:26:49,639
It may be a candle in a house, I then conjectured.

397
00:26:50,559 --> 00:26:53,000
But if so, I can never reach it.

398
00:26:53,580 --> 00:26:58,800
It is much too far away, and where it within a yard of me, what would it avail?

399
00:26:59,360 --> 00:27:02,160
I should but knock at the door to have it shut in my face.

400
00:27:04,160 --> 00:27:08,419
And I sank down where I stood and hid my face against the ground.

401
00:27:09,900 --> 00:27:11,279
I lay still a while.

402
00:27:11,980 --> 00:27:17,440
The night wind swept over the hill and over me, and died moaning in the distance.

403
00:27:18,419 --> 00:27:22,080
The rain fell fast, wetting me a fresh to the skin.

404
00:27:23,160 --> 00:27:25,860
Could I but have stiffened to the still frost?

405
00:27:26,779 --> 00:27:30,000
The friendly numbness of death, it might have pelted on.

406
00:27:30,599 --> 00:27:32,080
I should not have felt it.

407
00:27:32,819 --> 00:27:36,940
But my yet living flesh shuddered at its chilling influence.

408
00:27:37,940 --> 00:27:39,260
I rose there long.

409
00:27:39,900 --> 00:27:43,879
The light was yet there, shining dim but constant through the rain.

410
00:27:44,739 --> 00:27:45,959
I tried to walk again.

411
00:27:46,800 --> 00:27:49,900
I dragged my exhausted limbs slowly towards it.

412
00:27:50,300 --> 00:27:52,180
It led me a slant over the hill.

413
00:27:52,959 --> 00:27:57,099
Through a wide bog, which would have been impossible in winter,

414
00:27:57,101 --> 00:28:00,959
and was splashy and shaking even now, in the height of summer.

415
00:28:01,980 --> 00:28:03,239
Here I fell twice.

416
00:28:04,180 --> 00:28:06,900
But as often I rose and rallied my faculties.

417
00:28:07,639 --> 00:28:09,519
This light was my fore-lawn hope.

418
00:28:10,339 --> 00:28:11,379
I must gain it.

419
00:28:12,699 --> 00:28:16,779
Having crossed the marsh, I saw a trace of white over the more.

420
00:28:17,819 --> 00:28:18,819
I approached it.

421
00:28:19,360 --> 00:28:20,760
It was a road or a track.

422
00:28:21,419 --> 00:28:25,720
It led straight up to the light, which now beamed from a sort of knoll

423
00:28:25,720 --> 00:28:31,279
amidst a clump of trees, furs apparently, from what I could distinguish of the

424
00:28:31,281 --> 00:28:34,339
character of their forms and foliage through the gloom.

425
00:28:35,319 --> 00:28:37,720
My star vanished as I drew near.

426
00:28:38,599 --> 00:28:41,300
Some obstacle had intervened between me and it.

427
00:28:42,360 --> 00:28:45,760
I put out my hand to feel the dark mass before me.

428
00:28:46,940 --> 00:28:51,739
I discriminated the rough stones of a low wall above it, something like palisades,

429
00:28:52,260 --> 00:28:54,760
and within a high and prickly hedge.

430
00:28:55,319 --> 00:28:56,360
I grouped on.

431
00:28:57,180 --> 00:29:00,180
Again, a whitish object gleamed before me.

432
00:29:00,919 --> 00:29:02,459
It was a gate, a wicked.

433
00:29:03,139 --> 00:29:05,260
It moved on its hinges as I touched it.

434
00:29:05,959 --> 00:29:09,040
On each side stood a sable bush, holly or you.

435
00:29:10,339 --> 00:29:15,220
Entering the gate and passing the shrubs, the silhouette of a house rose to view

436
00:29:15,220 --> 00:29:20,139
black, low and rather long, but the guiding light shone nowhere.

437
00:29:20,660 --> 00:29:22,019
All was obscurity.

438
00:29:23,500 --> 00:29:25,339
Were the inmates retired to rest?

439
00:29:26,699 --> 00:29:28,000
I feared it must be so.

440
00:29:29,120 --> 00:29:31,879
In seeking the door, I turned an angle.

441
00:29:32,940 --> 00:29:37,300
They are shot out the friendly gleam again, from the lozenged pains of a very

442
00:29:37,300 --> 00:29:42,540
small lattice window within a foot of the ground, made still smaller by the growth

443
00:29:42,540 --> 00:29:48,540
of ivy or some other creeping plant, whose leaves clustered thick over the

444
00:29:48,540 --> 00:29:50,800
portion of the house wall in which it was set.

445
00:29:52,819 --> 00:29:56,285
The aperture was so screened and narrow that

446
00:29:56,286 --> 00:29:59,980
curtain or shutter had been deemed unnecessary.

447
00:30:01,080 --> 00:30:05,419
And when I stooped down and put aside the spray of foliage shooting over it,

448
00:30:06,080 --> 00:30:07,260
I could see all within.

449
00:30:08,239 --> 00:30:14,180
I could see clearly a room with a sanded floor, clean scoured, a dresser of walnut

450
00:30:14,180 --> 00:30:17,194
with pewter plates ranged in rows, reflecting

451
00:30:17,194 --> 00:30:20,279
the redness and radiance of a glowing pit fire.

452
00:30:21,559 --> 00:30:28,680
I could see a clock, a white deal table, some chairs, the candle whose ray had been

453
00:30:28,680 --> 00:30:34,440
my beacon, burnt on the table, and by its light, an elderly woman,

454
00:30:34,900 --> 00:30:38,521
somewhat rough looking, but scrupulously clean

455
00:30:38,523 --> 00:30:42,360
like all about her, was knitting a stocking.

456
00:30:43,099 --> 00:30:46,139
I noticed these objects cursually only.

457
00:30:47,360 --> 00:30:49,099
In them there was nothing extraordinary.

458
00:30:49,940 --> 00:30:53,713
A group of more interest appeared near the hearth, sitting

459
00:30:53,714 --> 00:30:57,199
still amidst the rosy piece and warmth suffusing it.

460
00:30:58,339 --> 00:31:04,080
Two young, graceful women, ladies in every point, sat one in a low rocking chair,

461
00:31:04,639 --> 00:31:06,000
the other on a lower stool.

462
00:31:07,080 --> 00:31:11,072
Both wore deep mourning of crape and bombazine, which

463
00:31:11,072 --> 00:31:14,620
somber garb singularly set off very fair necks and faces.

464
00:31:15,760 --> 00:31:20,540
A large old pointer dog rested its massive head on the knee of one girl.

465
00:31:21,480 --> 00:31:24,900
In the lap of the other was cushioned a black cat.

466
00:31:26,120 --> 00:31:31,000
A strange place was this humble kitchen for such occupants.

467
00:31:31,839 --> 00:31:32,839
Who were they?

468
00:31:33,860 --> 00:31:38,300
They could not be the daughters of the elderly person at the table, for she

469
00:31:38,300 --> 00:31:42,419
looked like a rustic, and they were all delicacy and cultivation.

470
00:31:43,739 --> 00:31:48,906
I had nowhere seen such faces as theirs, and yet, as I

471
00:31:48,906 --> 00:31:53,160
gazed on them, I seemed intimate with every liniment.

472
00:31:54,000 --> 00:31:55,379
I cannot call them handsome.

473
00:31:56,120 --> 00:31:58,080
They were too pale and grave for the word.

474
00:31:58,860 --> 00:32:03,260
As they each bent over a book, they looked thoughtful almost to severity.

475
00:32:04,199 --> 00:32:10,080
A stand between them supported a second candle and two great volumes, to which

476
00:32:10,080 --> 00:32:15,760
they frequently referred, comparing them seemingly with the smaller books they held

477
00:32:15,760 --> 00:32:18,235
in their hands, like people consulting a

478
00:32:18,235 --> 00:32:21,680
dictionary to aid them in the task of translation.

479
00:32:22,120 --> 00:32:26,377
This scene was as silent as if all the figures had

480
00:32:26,379 --> 00:32:30,220
been shadows and the fire lit apartment a picture.

481
00:32:31,000 --> 00:32:32,480
So hushed was it.

482
00:32:33,199 --> 00:32:38,239
I could hear the cinders fall from the grate, the clock tick in its obscure

483
00:32:38,241 --> 00:32:41,750
corner, and I even fancied I could distinguish

484
00:32:41,750 --> 00:32:44,900
the click-click of the woman's knitting needles.

485
00:32:45,760 --> 00:32:48,826
When, therefore, a voice broke the strange

486
00:32:48,826 --> 00:32:53,161
stillness at last, it was audible enough to me.

487
00:32:53,819 --> 00:32:56,879
Listen, Diana, said one of the absorbed students.

488
00:32:58,180 --> 00:33:02,879
France and Old Daniel are together in the night time, and France is telling a dream

489
00:33:02,881 --> 00:33:06,599
from which he has awakened in terror, listen.

490
00:33:07,779 --> 00:33:14,139
And in a low voice, she read something, of which not one word was intelligible to me.

491
00:33:14,900 --> 00:33:18,673
For it was in an unknown tongue, neither French nor

492
00:33:18,673 --> 00:33:22,300
Latin, whether it were Greek or German, I could not tell.

493
00:33:23,360 --> 00:33:27,040
That is strong, she said, when she had finished.

494
00:33:27,739 --> 00:33:28,839
I relish it.

495
00:33:29,860 --> 00:33:35,760
The other girl, who had lifted her head to listen to her sister, repeated while she

496
00:33:35,760 --> 00:33:39,300
gazed at the fire, a line of what had been read.

497
00:33:40,180 --> 00:33:43,760
At a later day, I knew the language and the book.

498
00:33:44,459 --> 00:33:47,019
Therefore, I will hear, quote, the line.

499
00:33:48,239 --> 00:33:53,379
Though when I first heard it, it was only like a stroke on sounding brass to me,

500
00:33:54,120 --> 00:33:55,160
conveying no meaning.

501
00:33:56,660 --> 00:34:00,919
Da trat hevo Ina, anzu sehenvidee stern ennucked.

502
00:34:01,639 --> 00:34:06,360
Good, good, she exclaimed, while her dark and deep eyes sparkled.

503
00:34:07,199 --> 00:34:11,419
There you have a dim and mighty archangel fitly set before you.

504
00:34:12,199 --> 00:34:14,620
The line is worth a hundred pages afustian.

505
00:34:16,059 --> 00:34:19,972
Ich wager dae, geranken, in der Schale minus, zornes

506
00:34:19,972 --> 00:34:22,660
und dae, werke mit dem gervisch -de-minus grims.

507
00:34:23,639 --> 00:34:26,260
I like it, both were again silent.

508
00:34:27,760 --> 00:34:30,599
Is there only country where they talk of that way?

509
00:34:31,540 --> 00:34:34,720
Asked the old woman, looking up from her knitting.

510
00:34:35,599 --> 00:34:41,959
Yes, Hannah, a far larger country than England, where they talk in no other way.

511
00:34:43,040 --> 00:34:47,279
Well, for sure case, I naunt how they can understand to one other.

512
00:34:48,120 --> 00:34:52,839
And if either of you went there, you could tell what they said, I guess.

513
00:34:53,279 --> 00:34:57,879
We could probably tell something of what they said, but not all.

514
00:34:58,680 --> 00:35:04,319
For we are not as clever as you think us, Hannah, we don't speak German and we

515
00:35:04,321 --> 00:35:07,180
cannot read it without a dictionary to help us.

516
00:35:08,580 --> 00:35:10,580
And what good does it do you?

517
00:35:11,959 --> 00:35:15,839
We mean to teach it some time, or at least the elements as they say,

518
00:35:16,800 --> 00:35:19,220
and then we shall get more money than we do now.

519
00:35:20,639 --> 00:35:24,739
Very like, but give our studying, you've done for tonight.

520
00:35:25,699 --> 00:35:28,440
I think we have, at least I'm tired.

521
00:35:29,319 --> 00:35:30,419
Mary, are you?

522
00:35:31,739 --> 00:35:34,502
Mortally, after all, it's tough work, fagging

523
00:35:34,504 --> 00:35:37,601
away at a language with no master but a lexicon.

524
00:35:38,339 --> 00:35:42,959
It is, especially such a language as this crabbed but glorious Deutsche.

525
00:35:43,940 --> 00:35:45,800
I wonder when Sinjin will come home.

526
00:35:47,500 --> 00:35:51,091
Surely he will not be long now, it is just ten,

527
00:35:51,091 --> 00:35:54,360
looking at a little gold what she drew from her girdle.

528
00:35:55,099 --> 00:35:56,819
It rains fast, Hannah.

529
00:35:57,639 --> 00:36:00,120
Will you have the goodness to look at the fire in the parlour?

530
00:36:01,319 --> 00:36:02,559
The woman rose.

531
00:36:03,660 --> 00:36:07,040
She opened a door, through which I dimly saw a passage.

532
00:36:07,919 --> 00:36:11,260
Soon I heard her stir a fire in an inner room.

533
00:36:11,800 --> 00:36:13,019
She presently came back.

534
00:36:13,739 --> 00:36:16,239
Ah, a children, said she.

535
00:36:16,800 --> 00:36:19,239
It fear troubles me to go into a young room now.

536
00:36:20,300 --> 00:36:24,220
It looks so lonesome with the chair empty and set back in a corner.

537
00:36:25,480 --> 00:36:27,099
She wiped her eyes with her apron.

538
00:36:27,860 --> 00:36:31,620
The two girls, grave before, looked sad now.

539
00:36:32,919 --> 00:36:36,500
But he is in a better place, continued Hannah.

540
00:36:37,160 --> 00:36:40,269
We shouldn't wish him here again, and then

541
00:36:40,269 --> 00:36:44,019
nobody need to have acquired a death nor he had.

542
00:36:45,400 --> 00:36:49,099
You say he never mentioned us, inquired one of the ladies.

543
00:36:50,260 --> 00:36:51,319
He hadn't time, Ben.

544
00:36:51,900 --> 00:36:53,559
He was gone in a minute was your father.

545
00:36:54,339 --> 00:36:58,360
He had been a bit ailing like the day before, but not to signify.

546
00:36:59,500 --> 00:37:03,178
And when Mr. Sinjin asked if he would like either

547
00:37:03,180 --> 00:37:06,480
a key to be sent for, he fair laughed at him.

548
00:37:07,360 --> 00:37:11,760
He began again with a bit of a heaviness in his head the next day.

549
00:37:12,500 --> 00:37:14,559
That is, a fortnight sin.

550
00:37:15,459 --> 00:37:18,000
And he went to sleep and never wakened.

551
00:37:18,860 --> 00:37:23,080
He were almost stuck when your brother went into the chamber and found him.

552
00:37:24,199 --> 00:37:27,419
Ah, children, that's the last of the old stock.

553
00:37:28,260 --> 00:37:32,019
For ye and Mr. Sinjin is like of different sort to them, it's gone.

554
00:37:33,279 --> 00:37:36,940
For all your mother-worm is she your way, and a most as book learned.

555
00:37:37,779 --> 00:37:39,300
She were the picture or your Mary.

556
00:37:40,580 --> 00:37:42,279
Diana is more like your father.

557
00:37:43,620 --> 00:37:48,044
I thought them so similar, I could not tell where the old

558
00:37:48,044 --> 00:37:52,519
servant, for such I now concluded her to be, saw the difference.

559
00:37:53,959 --> 00:37:57,180
Both were fair, complexion and slenderly made.

560
00:37:58,360 --> 00:38:01,739
Both possessed faces full of distinction and intelligence.

561
00:38:02,800 --> 00:38:06,197
One to be sure had hair a shade darker than the other,

562
00:38:06,199 --> 00:38:09,279
and there was a difference in their style of wearing it.

563
00:38:10,239 --> 00:38:13,779
Mary's pale brown locks were parted and braided smooth.

564
00:38:14,720 --> 00:38:18,459
Diana's dusky attresses covered her neck with thick curls.

565
00:38:19,459 --> 00:38:21,000
The clock struck ten.

566
00:38:22,620 --> 00:38:27,686
You'll want your supper, I am sure, observed Hannah, and so will Mr.

567
00:38:27,686 --> 00:38:29,180
Sinjin when he comes in.

568
00:38:30,059 --> 00:38:32,440
And she proceeded to prepare the meal.

569
00:38:33,639 --> 00:38:34,639
The ladies rose.

570
00:38:35,300 --> 00:38:37,379
They seemed about to withdraw to the parlor.

571
00:38:38,040 --> 00:38:41,639
Till this moment, I had been so intent on watching them.

572
00:38:42,580 --> 00:38:47,000
Their appearance and conversation had excited in me so keen and interest.

573
00:38:47,940 --> 00:38:50,660
I had half forgotten my own wretched position.

574
00:38:51,180 --> 00:38:52,459
Now it recurred to me.

575
00:38:53,180 --> 00:38:56,819
More desolate, more desperate than ever it seemed from contrast.

576
00:38:57,699 --> 00:39:03,440
And how impossible did it appear to touch the inmates of this house with concern on

577
00:39:03,440 --> 00:39:09,620
my behalf, to make them believe in the truth of my wants and woes, to induce them

578
00:39:09,620 --> 00:39:12,877
to vouch safe arrest for my wanderings, as I

579
00:39:12,879 --> 00:39:16,620
groped out the door and knocked at it hesitatingly.

580
00:39:16,940 --> 00:39:19,680
I felt that last idea to be a mere Kimmerer.

581
00:39:20,839 --> 00:39:21,839
Hannah opened.

582
00:39:23,680 --> 00:39:24,739
What do you want?

583
00:39:25,419 --> 00:39:27,752
She inquired in a voice of surprise, as she

584
00:39:27,752 --> 00:39:30,500
surveyed me by the light of the candle she held.

585
00:39:31,580 --> 00:39:33,959
May I speak to your mistresses, I said.

586
00:39:34,639 --> 00:39:36,720
You had better tell me what you have to say to them.

587
00:39:37,379 --> 00:39:38,379
Where do you come from?

588
00:39:39,319 --> 00:39:40,319
I am a stranger.

589
00:39:41,599 --> 00:39:43,400
What is your business here at this hour?

590
00:39:44,440 --> 00:39:50,440
I want a night's shelter in an outhouse or anywhere, and a morsel of bread to eat.

591
00:39:51,540 --> 00:39:55,459
Distrust, the very feeling I dreaded, appeared in Hannah's face.

592
00:39:56,959 --> 00:40:00,180
I'll give you a piece of bread, she said, after a pause.

593
00:40:00,879 --> 00:40:02,480
But we can't take in a vagrant to lodge.

594
00:40:03,059 --> 00:40:04,059
It isn't likely.

595
00:40:05,379 --> 00:40:06,779
Do let me speak to your mistresses.

596
00:40:07,980 --> 00:40:09,279
No, not I.

597
00:40:10,279 --> 00:40:11,440
What can they do for you?

598
00:40:11,440 --> 00:40:13,879
You should not be roving about now.

599
00:40:14,180 --> 00:40:15,239
It looks very ill.

600
00:40:16,279 --> 00:40:18,120
But where shall I go if you drive me away?

601
00:40:18,660 --> 00:40:19,660
What shall I do?

602
00:40:20,680 --> 00:40:23,660
Oh, I'll warrant you know where to go and what to do.

603
00:40:24,699 --> 00:40:26,819
Mind you don't do wrong, that's all.

604
00:40:27,500 --> 00:40:28,500
Here is a penny.

605
00:40:28,599 --> 00:40:29,599
Now go.

606
00:40:30,199 --> 00:40:34,160
A penny cannot feed me, and I have no strength to go farther.

607
00:40:34,440 --> 00:40:35,440
Don't shut the door.

608
00:40:35,559 --> 00:40:36,839
Oh, don't for God's sake.

609
00:40:38,000 --> 00:40:39,000
I must.

610
00:40:39,559 --> 00:40:41,000
The rain is driving in.

611
00:40:42,379 --> 00:40:45,000
Tell the young ladies, let me see them.

612
00:40:45,900 --> 00:40:46,959
Indeed, I will not.

613
00:40:47,879 --> 00:40:51,660
You are not what you ought to be, or you wouldn't make such a noise.

614
00:40:52,360 --> 00:40:53,360
Move off.

615
00:40:53,980 --> 00:40:55,739
But I must die if I'm turned away.

616
00:40:56,720 --> 00:40:57,720
Not you.

617
00:40:58,500 --> 00:41:01,302
I'm feared you have some ill plans again that bring

618
00:41:01,303 --> 00:41:04,120
you about folks' houses at this time of night.

619
00:41:04,699 --> 00:41:09,847
If you have any followers, housebreakers or such like, anywhere

620
00:41:09,847 --> 00:41:13,139
near, you may tell them we are not by ourselves in the house.

621
00:41:13,980 --> 00:41:17,440
We have a gentleman, and dogs, and guns.

622
00:41:18,680 --> 00:41:23,580
Hear the honest but inflexible servant clapped the door to and bolted it within.

623
00:41:24,360 --> 00:41:29,760
This was the climax, a pang of exquisite suffering, a throw of true despair,

624
00:41:30,339 --> 00:41:31,839
rent and heaved my heart.

625
00:41:32,519 --> 00:41:35,680
Worn out indeed I was, not another step could I stir.

626
00:41:36,480 --> 00:41:42,139
I sank on the wet doorstep, I groaned, I rung my hands, I wept in utter anguish.

627
00:41:42,940 --> 00:41:44,459
Oh, this specter of death.

628
00:41:45,319 --> 00:41:48,879
Oh, this last hour, approaching in such horror.

629
00:41:49,660 --> 00:41:53,599
Alas, this isolation, this banishment from my kind.

630
00:41:54,540 --> 00:41:58,339
Not only the anchor of hope, but the footing of fortitude was gone,

631
00:41:58,839 --> 00:41:59,860
at least for a moment.

632
00:42:00,419 --> 00:42:02,940
But the last I soon endeavoured to regain.

633
00:42:03,919 --> 00:42:07,680
I can but die, I said, and I believe in God.

634
00:42:08,599 --> 00:42:10,519
Let me try to wait his will in silence.

635
00:42:11,519 --> 00:42:17,379
These words, I not only thought, but uttered, and thrusting back all my

636
00:42:17,381 --> 00:42:22,959
misery into my heart, I made an effort to compel it to remain there, dumb and still.

637
00:42:24,080 --> 00:42:29,105
All men must die, said a voice quite close at hand, but all

638
00:42:29,105 --> 00:42:32,500
are not condemned to meet a lingering and premature doom.

639
00:42:33,300 --> 00:42:36,540
Such as yours would be if you perished here of want.

640
00:42:37,599 --> 00:42:44,319
Who or what speaks, I asked, terrified at the unexpected sound, and incapable now of

641
00:42:44,321 --> 00:42:47,220
deriving from any occurrence a hope of aid.

642
00:42:47,959 --> 00:42:52,027
A form was near, what form, the pitch-dark knight and

643
00:42:52,027 --> 00:42:55,279
my infeebled vision prevented me from distinguishing.

644
00:42:55,940 --> 00:43:00,059
With a loud, long knock, the newcomer appealed to the door.

645
00:43:01,099 --> 00:43:02,400
Is it you, Mr. Shingin?

646
00:43:02,720 --> 00:43:05,879
cried Hannah, yes, yes, open quickly.

647
00:43:06,940 --> 00:43:10,900
Well, how wet and cold you must be, such a wild night as it is.

648
00:43:11,639 --> 00:43:13,978
Come in, your sisters are quite uneasy about

649
00:43:13,978 --> 00:43:16,821
you and I believe there are bad folks about.

650
00:43:17,319 --> 00:43:18,900
There has been a beggar woman.

651
00:43:19,720 --> 00:43:21,440
I declare she has not gone yet.

652
00:43:22,339 --> 00:43:23,339
Lay down there.

653
00:43:23,480 --> 00:43:24,480
Get up for shame.

654
00:43:25,040 --> 00:43:26,040
Move off, I say.

655
00:43:27,419 --> 00:43:28,419
Hush, Hannah.

656
00:43:29,080 --> 00:43:30,660
I have a word to say to the woman.

657
00:43:31,500 --> 00:43:33,500
You have done your duty in excluding.

658
00:43:34,199 --> 00:43:36,139
Now let me do mine in admitting her.

659
00:43:36,480 --> 00:43:39,300
I was near and listened to both you and her.

660
00:43:39,919 --> 00:43:41,919
I think this is a peculiar case.

661
00:43:42,559 --> 00:43:43,860
I must at least examine into it.

662
00:43:44,500 --> 00:43:48,139
Young woman, rise and pass before me into the house.

663
00:43:49,620 --> 00:43:51,319
With difficulty, I obeyed him.

664
00:43:52,699 --> 00:43:57,199
Presently, I stood within that clean, bright kitchen on the very hearth,

665
00:43:57,779 --> 00:43:59,180
trembling, sickening.

666
00:44:00,059 --> 00:44:05,220
Conscious of an aspect in the last degree, ghastly wild and weather-beaten.

667
00:44:06,120 --> 00:44:14,080
The two ladies, their brother, Mr. Sinjin, the old servant, were all gazing at me.

668
00:44:15,540 --> 00:44:17,500
Sinjin, who is it?

669
00:44:17,900 --> 00:44:18,900
I heard one ask.

670
00:44:19,419 --> 00:44:20,419
I cannot tell.

671
00:44:20,720 --> 00:44:22,839
I found her at the door was the reply.

672
00:44:23,639 --> 00:44:29,580
She does look white, said Hannah, as white as clay or death was responded.

673
00:44:30,360 --> 00:44:33,798
She will fall, let her sit, and indeed my

674
00:44:33,800 --> 00:44:37,319
head swam, I dropped but a chair received me.

675
00:44:38,139 --> 00:44:41,660
I still possessed my senses, though just now I could not speak.

676
00:44:43,000 --> 00:44:44,959
Perhaps a little water would restore her.

677
00:44:45,559 --> 00:44:46,680
Hannah, fetch some.

678
00:44:47,839 --> 00:44:49,120
But she is worn to nothing.

679
00:44:49,739 --> 00:44:52,040
How very thin and how very bloodless.

680
00:44:52,800 --> 00:44:54,519
A mere specter.

681
00:44:55,620 --> 00:44:57,300
Is she ill or only famished?

682
00:44:58,180 --> 00:44:59,180
Famished, I think.

683
00:44:59,879 --> 00:45:01,379
Hannah, is that milk?

684
00:45:02,120 --> 00:45:03,419
Give it me in a piece of bread.

685
00:45:04,839 --> 00:45:10,319
Diana, I knew her by the long curls which I saw drooping between me and the fire as

686
00:45:10,321 --> 00:45:14,540
she bent over me, broke some bread, dipped it in milk and put it to my lips.

687
00:45:15,379 --> 00:45:16,559
Her face was near mine.

688
00:45:17,319 --> 00:45:21,400
I saw there was pity in it, and I felt sympathy in her hurried breathing.

689
00:45:22,180 --> 00:45:25,720
In her simple words too, the same balm like emotion spoke.

690
00:45:27,040 --> 00:45:28,040
Try to eat.

691
00:45:29,160 --> 00:45:32,339
Yes, try, repeated Mary gently.

692
00:45:33,059 --> 00:45:36,379
A Mary's hand removed my sodden bonnet and lifted my head.

693
00:45:37,260 --> 00:45:40,919
I tasted what they offered me, feebly at first, eagerly soon.

694
00:45:41,739 --> 00:45:44,860
Not too much at first, restrain her, said the brother.

695
00:45:44,860 --> 00:45:49,379
She has had enough, and he withdrew the cup of milk and the plate of bread.

696
00:45:50,419 --> 00:45:54,519
A little more syngin, look at the airvidity in her eyes.

697
00:45:55,760 --> 00:45:56,839
No more at present, sister.

698
00:45:57,419 --> 00:45:59,720
Try if she can speak now, ask her her name.

699
00:46:00,839 --> 00:46:05,459
I felt I could speak, and I answered, my name is Jane Elliott.

700
00:46:07,540 --> 00:46:13,160
Anxious as ever to avoid discovery, I had before resolved to assume an alias.

701
00:46:14,139 --> 00:46:15,300
And where do you live?

702
00:46:16,099 --> 00:46:17,099
Where are your friends?

703
00:46:17,699 --> 00:46:18,699
I was silent.

704
00:46:19,139 --> 00:46:20,760
Can we send for anyone you know?

705
00:46:21,319 --> 00:46:22,319
I shook my head.

706
00:46:23,080 --> 00:46:25,040
What account can you give of yourself?

707
00:46:26,599 --> 00:46:32,080
Somehow, now that I had once crossed the threshold of this house, and once was

708
00:46:32,080 --> 00:46:37,199
brought face-to-face with its owners, I felt no longer outcast, vagrant,

709
00:46:37,559 --> 00:46:39,500
and disowned by the wide world.

710
00:46:40,260 --> 00:46:45,339
I dared to put off the mendicant, to resume my natural manner and character.

711
00:46:45,959 --> 00:46:51,160
I began once more to know myself, and when Mr. Syngin demanded an account,

712
00:46:51,779 --> 00:46:56,599
which at present I was far too weak to render, I said after a brief pause.

713
00:46:57,260 --> 00:47:00,540
Sir, I can give you no details tonight.

714
00:47:01,459 --> 00:47:04,760
But what then said he, do you expect me to do for you?

715
00:47:05,519 --> 00:47:07,000
Nothing, I replied.

716
00:47:07,819 --> 00:47:09,839
My strength suffice for but short answers.

717
00:47:10,919 --> 00:47:11,919
Diana took the word.

718
00:47:12,879 --> 00:47:17,199
Do you mean, she asked, that we have now given you what aid you require,

719
00:47:17,839 --> 00:47:21,419
and that we may dismiss you to the more and the rainy night?

720
00:47:22,220 --> 00:47:23,360
I looked at her.

721
00:47:24,220 --> 00:47:31,620
She had, I thought, a remarkable countenance, instinct both with power and goodness.

722
00:47:31,680 --> 00:47:33,139
I took sudden courage.

723
00:47:34,319 --> 00:47:39,300
Answering her compassionate gaze with a smile, I said, I will trust you.

724
00:47:40,239 --> 00:47:43,150
If I were a masterless and stray dog, I know that

725
00:47:43,152 --> 00:47:45,661
you would not turn me from your heart tonight.

726
00:47:46,519 --> 00:47:48,580
As it is, I really have no fear.

727
00:47:49,660 --> 00:47:52,000
Do with me and for me as you like.

728
00:47:52,959 --> 00:47:54,459
But excuse me from much discourse.

729
00:47:55,239 --> 00:47:56,239
My breath is short.

730
00:47:56,720 --> 00:47:58,180
I feel a spasm when I speak.

731
00:47:58,940 --> 00:48:02,120
All three surveyed me and all three were silent.

732
00:48:03,639 --> 00:48:06,199
Hannah said Mr. Sinjin at last.

733
00:48:07,099 --> 00:48:10,480
Let her sit there at present and ask her no questions.

734
00:48:10,959 --> 00:48:14,319
In ten minutes more, give her the remainder of that milk and bread.

735
00:48:15,360 --> 00:48:19,680
Mary and Diana, let us go into the parlour and talk the matter over.

736
00:48:21,400 --> 00:48:22,540
They withdrew.

737
00:48:23,580 --> 00:48:25,919
Very soon, one of the ladies returned.

738
00:48:26,739 --> 00:48:28,139
I could not tell which.

739
00:48:28,980 --> 00:48:34,059
A kind of pleasant stupor was stealing over me as I sat by the genial fire.

740
00:48:35,120 --> 00:48:37,779
In an undertone, she gave some directions to Hannah.

741
00:48:39,139 --> 00:48:43,680
Air long, with the servants aid, I contrived to mount a staircase.

742
00:48:44,580 --> 00:48:45,900
My dripping clothes were removed.

743
00:48:46,580 --> 00:48:49,580
Soon, a warm dry bed received me.

744
00:48:50,500 --> 00:48:54,254
I thanked God, experienced amidst unutterable

745
00:48:54,254 --> 00:48:58,800
exhaustion, a glow of grateful joy, and slept.
